/-!
# Small tables for the binary linear action

The coordinate action preserves XOR. Splitting an eleven-bit mask into its low
five and high six bits therefore reduces the action comparison to tables of
length 32 and 64. The packed tables are checked against the original row action
in each native validation block; no arithmetic output is trusted.
-/
